Workstation SLURM: a record of every job, without an accounting database. SLURM's job
completion plugins are told when each run of a job ends (finished, failed, cancelled, including
while pending, or requeued), but not when it's submitted. This adds that: a submit event, sent
once the job's record exists (so it has its id; the job_submit plugins run before that), and
not for --test-only. Only jobcomp/script acts on it: it runs JobCompLoc (bin/job_record) for
submissions too, with EVENT=submit or EVENT=end in its environment. CLUSTER falls back to
ClusterName (it otherwise comes from accounting). Applied by build.sh; see SLURM/Setup.md.

The other plugins that implement record_job_start (elasticsearch, kafka, lua, mysql) would take
a submit event for a start; none of them is built here.

diff -ru a/src/interfaces/jobcomp.c b/src/interfaces/jobcomp.c
--- a/src/interfaces/jobcomp.c
+++ b/src/interfaces/jobcomp.c
@@ -226,3 +226,21 @@
 	slurm_mutex_unlock(&context_lock);
 	return retval;
 }
+
+extern int jobcomp_g_record_job_submit(job_record_t *job_ptr)
+{
+	int retval = SLURM_SUCCESS;
+
+	xassert(plugin_inited != PLUGIN_NOT_INITED);
+
+	if (plugin_inited == PLUGIN_NOOP)
+		return SLURM_SUCCESS;
+
+	slurm_mutex_lock(&context_lock);
+
+	xassert(g_context);
+	retval = (*(ops.record_job_start))(job_ptr, JOBCOMP_EVENT_JOB_SUBMIT);
+
+	slurm_mutex_unlock(&context_lock);
+	return retval;
+}
